{"scenario": "perf/a-1-mib-request-line", "requires": ["v1", "fake-backend", "perf"], "doc": "The baseline of the largest request: a line of about 1 MiB (the client limit) read and decoded, its largest forwardable part re-encoded, forwarded to the backend and answered, 20 times (--perf records every sample, no budget). The vehicle is env/set, the one method the backend still serves (agents/* are the hub's own since agent system part 1): 16 values of 32 KiB (its limits) and a 500 KB key it does not know, dropped and listed in the answer."}
{"do": "start", "hub": "h", "env": {"DRGNX_FAKE_BACKEND_SCRIPT": "{\"env/set\": {\"result\": {\"applied\": []}}}"}}
{"do": "connect", "conn": "c", "hub": "h"}
